{"_id":"6925a80c7c7d1fa20e7693f1","roadmapSlug":"elasticsearch","nodeId":"Avit-NGMkIA9JwJ7OUiNZ","description":"# Avg, Sum, Min, and Max Aggregations\n\nThese aggregations are fundamental tools for calculating statistical summaries of numerical data. They compute the average (Avg), total (Sum), smallest value (Min), and largest value (Max) respectively, across a set of documents that match a query. These aggregations operate on numeric fields within your Elasticsearch indices, providing insights into the distribution and range of your data.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Aggregations","url":"https://www.elastic.co/docs/explore-analyze/query-filter/aggregations","_id":"69284397467651eddb61af42"},{"type":"official","title":"Avg aggregation","url":"https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/aggregations/search-aggregations-metrics-avg-aggregation","_id":"69284397467651eddb61af43"},{"type":"official","title":"Sum aggregation","url":"https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/aggregations/search-aggregations-metrics-sum-aggregation","_id":"69284397467651eddb61af44"},{"type":"official","title":"Max aggregation","url":"https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/aggregations/search-aggregations-metrics-max-aggregation","_id":"69284397467651eddb61af45"},{"type":"official","title":"Min aggregation","url":"https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/aggregations/search-aggregations-metrics-min-aggregation","_id":"69284397467651eddb61af46"},{"type":"article","title":"A Basic Guide To Elasticsearch Aggregations","url":"https://logz.io/blog/elasticsearch-aggregations/","_id":"69284397467651eddb61af47"},{"type":"article","title":"ElasticSearch Aggregation & Queries","url":"https://medium.com/@souravchoudhary0306/elasticsearch-aggregation-queries-557131ef5ea4","_id":"69284397467651eddb61af48"},{"type":"video","title":"Learn about elastic search aggregation in 15 minutes","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZziIEDfA8ZE","_id":"69284397467651eddb61af49"}],"createdAt":"2025-11-25T12:58:52.68